      "Large import cases rarely begin with a glamorous set-piece. They begin with a driver, a burger van, members of the public who dial 999, and officers who treat an odd container break-in as more than roadside theft. Furniture-parts cover stories and holdalls in the wrong place are classic concealment patterns; spotting them still depends on someone noticing and reporting.",
      "From that Northampton tip-off, investigators mapped a conspiracy that stretched well beyond one county. National tracing matters because cocaine importation networks are built to fragment: different people handle logistics, storage, distribution and money. A six-month headline seizure is the visible spike; the charging timeline is the longer spine.",
