    paragraphs: [
      'University tuition fees for European students have become an important issue in ongoing discussions between the United Kingdom and the European Union, potentially affecting wider efforts to improve relations after Brexit.',
      'Several EU member states are reportedly seeking a clearer commitment from the British government before the planned November summit. Their preference is for eligible European students to have access to tuition fees closer to the rates paid by domestic students in the UK, rather than the higher international fees introduced following Brexit.',
      'For many students, the difference could have a substantial impact on whether studying at a British university is financially realistic.',
      { style: 'h2', text: 'Why the tuition fee disagreement matters' },
      "Before Brexit, students from EU countries generally benefited from the same tuition fee arrangements as UK students in England. Following the UK's departure from the European Union, most new EU students became subject to international student fee arrangements.",
      'International tuition fees can be considerably higher, depending on the university and course.',
      'European representatives are concerned that the increased costs could discourage young people from studying in the UK and reduce educational and cultural connections between the two sides.',
      'Some member states are therefore pushing for the issue to be addressed as part of the wider negotiations rather than postponed until a later stage.',
      { style: 'h2', text: 'Wider agreements could be affected' },
      'The tuition fee discussions are taking place alongside negotiations covering several other areas of UK-EU cooperation.',
      'These include plans to simplify trade in food and agricultural products, reconnect carbon trading arrangements and develop opportunities for younger people to live, work and study across Europe and the UK.',
      'The proposed youth exchange arrangements are particularly important to EU officials seeking to rebuild opportunities for young people following Brexit.',
      'There are concerns that disagreements over student fees could slow progress on some of these wider agreements.',
      { style: 'h2', text: 'UK and EU also discuss industrial cooperation' },
      'Beyond education and trade, both sides are considering closer cooperation in strategically important industries, including steel and defence.',
      "The UK is also interested in participating in the EU's proposed industrial policy framework, which could influence access to public contracts and support for European manufacturing.",
      'However, discussions around the framework remain ongoing, with different member states holding different positions on which international partners should qualify.',
      { style: 'h2', text: 'What happens next?' },
      'The planned November summit is expected to provide an opportunity for UK and EU leaders to discuss the outstanding issues and identify areas where agreements can be reached.',
      'For prospective university students, the outcome could influence the future cost of studying in Britain. However, until a formal agreement is announced, existing tuition fee arrangements should not be assumed to have changed.',
    ],
